      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Alkanes are saturated hydrocarbons with the general formula CₙH₂ₙ₊₂. Methane (CH₄) is the simplest member of this family. The homologous series of alkanes with condensed structural formulae and molecular formulae are shown in Table 11.1.",
            "bold": [
              "Table 11.1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "note",
            "title": "Did You Know?",
            "text": "Butane is a fuel used in lighters. Isobutane is used as a propellant in products such as shaving gel."
          },
          {
